sequenceDiagram
  %% Private Node store: one named running container, no Process actions.
  %% status: draft
  %% command: instance:runtime:update
  %% kind: instance.runtime_update
  autonumber
  %% lane CLI icon=terminal pill=caller tone=gray
  %% lane GW icon=gateway pill=intent tone=blue
  %% lane SW icon=workflow pill=executes tone=green
  %% lane N icon=server pill=target tone=amber
  participant CLI as CLI / MCP<br/>orbit · MCP tools
  participant GW as Gateway<br/>Laravel API
  participant SW as Swamp<br/>workflow execution
  participant N as app-dev Node<br/>Instance container
  CLI->>GW: instance:runtime:update ID
  %%> Command:
  %%> - `orbit instance:runtime:update INSTANCE`
  %%> - syntax: `[instance-id] [--json]`; omitted interactive input uses the Instance picker; cancellation starts no Operation
  Note over GW: Admit runtime update
  %%> When:
  %%> - the named Instance is active, has a running development container and has no lifecycle or Process operation in progress; hold its Instance lock
  %%> On failure:
  %%> - a checkout, non-development placement, stopped container or busy Instance refuses with existing codes and starts no run
  GW->>SW: Start run, full intent<br/>operation-instance-runtime-update
  GW-->>CLI: 202 Accepted<br/>Operation ID
  SW->>N: Prepare Node runtimes<br/>Ansible · tags node-runtime
  %%> What it does:
  %%> - first requires this release’s shared runtime identity and executable Vite+ before any store change; then atomically converts the old shared-store link to a private copy; Vite+ resolves each Process working directory and fetches only a missing resolved Node
  %%> - the phase is bounded at 150 seconds; resolution and downloads share 90 seconds; no Process is stopped, started or restarted
  alt store changed
    %% path: main
    N-->>SW: Converted store<br/>versions · pins
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
  else already prepared
    %% path: repeat
    N-->>SW: Unchanged store<br/>versions · pins
    SW-->>GW: Run succeeded<br/>terminal result
  else preparation failed
    %% path: failed
    N--xSW: Node preparation failed
    %%> On failure:
    %%> - instance.runtime_prerequisite_failed keeps the old store on a missing/mismatched shared runtime; instance.node_runtime_prepare_failed names the pin and reason; completed copies stay; the owner may repeat; Processes remain as they were
    SW--xGW: Run failed<br/>error code
  end
  loop until terminal
    CLI->>GW: operation:show TASK
    GW-->>CLI: Status and result
  end
